MID_LGV_0XXX_c01_GM00_003_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c01_GM00_003_m01_001: Surely... Surely it cannot be much further to the\nforbidden land...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c01_GM00_003_m01_002: Thanks for bearing with me. The village is a little\nways north of here, across the desert wall.
LGV_0XXX_c01_GM00_003_m01_Footer: <TEDF>
MID_LGV_LG00_001_Statue_Kai: <DLG>Cai Castor\nA youth from Ribeira village. His superior athleticism and superb\nspear skills made him a standout in the Heroic Games. Moreover,\nhis left hand gave him the unusual power to set distant things\naflame and see the invisible. This statue was erected in honor\nof his appearance in the main matches of the Heroic Games in\nthe year 1449.
MID_LGV_LG00_001_Statue_Dit: <DLG>Dietrich Gregor Lamine\nA black-clad swordsman from the land of Fódlan. His striking\nappearance captivated all who saw him. The cloak he wore gave\nhim the strange power to walk from shadow to shadow, instilling\nfear in many of his opponents. This statue was erected in honor\nof his appearance in the main matches of the Heroic Games in\nthe year 1449.
MID_LGV_LG00_001_Statue_Seo: <DLG>Theodora Sergio Savangren\nThe young queen of Saramis, which was known as the Shield of\nDagda. Stern and noble, she was beloved by her people. Her right\narm possessed peerless strength, enough to crush rocks or shields\nwith her bare hands. This statue was erected in honor of her\nappearance in the main matches of the Heroic Games in\nthe year 1449.
MID_LGV_LG00_001_Statue_Led: <DLG>Leda\nThough her true name and origin are unknown, she was thought to be\nconnected to Kalla's temple in some way. Her vihuela performances\nwere unmatched for skill and passion, stealing the hearts of her\naudiences. This statue was erected in honor of her appearance\nin the main matches of the Heroic Games in the year 1449.
MID_LGV_LG00_001_Statue_Bel: <DLG>The White-Maned Demon\nAn Aragonian whose true name was Bertrand, though he was better\nknown to the citizens of Dagsion as the White-Maned Demon. His axe\nconferred tremendous power and was believed to have belonged to\na previous king of Arago. This statue was erected in honor of his\nappearance in the main matches of the Heroic Games in the year 1449.
MID_LGV_LG00_001_Statue_Tal: <DLG>Talimun Vandahl\nSon of Vandahl, the Swashbuckler King, and the chief executive of\nthe Vandahl Trading Company, which is famed throughout Dagda.\nHe was a skilled sorcerer who often used a compass that pointed him\ndirectly to his desires. This statue was erected in honor of his\nappearance in the main matches of the Heroic Games in the year 1449.
MID_LGV_LG00_001_Statue_Orh: <DLG>Orchel\nA lead priest of Credna's temple. She was a secretive woman who hid\nher true face behind a cat mask. Oddly, flagstones she trod on broke\nas if shattering beneath the hooves of a giant kusarik. This statue was\nerected in honor of her appearance in the main matches of the\nHeroic Games in the year 1449.
MID_LGV_LG00_001_Statue_Anh: <DLG>Anatolia\nAn enigmatic figure from the west. Known as the "Mystery Bride," she\nwon over the hearts of Dagsion's citizens. She employed strange\nmartial arts, weapons that spit fire, and an unusual brand of spirit\nmagic to manipulate stone. This statue was erected in honor of her\nappearance in the main matches of the Heroic Games in the year 1449.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m01_001: I'm working on activating Nuwa's teleportation\ndevice, but it's not going well.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m01_002: The damage to its mass conversion reactor is worse\nthan I hoped. The output isn't near what it needs.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m01_003: This can't be a permanent solution, but I'm going to\ntry hooking it up to my own Heart Core.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m01_004: Sorry, but you might have to kill some time here.\nThere must be something around to interest you.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m02_001: Sorry for the delay. It wasn't easy, but I finally\nmanaged to activate the teleportation device.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m02_002: We can depart whenever you're ready. Just let\nme know.
MID_LGV_0XXX_LG00_002_m11: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_LG00_002_m11_001: Found something mechanical, have you? Let me\ntake a look.
MID_LGV_0XXX_LG00_002_m11_002: An upgraded Salamander... I'm surprised any of\nthese were left behind.
MID_LGV_0XXX_LG00_002_m11_003: They were once standard issue in the village\nof Kunlun.
MID_LGV_0XXX_LG00_002_m11_004: Mind if I take it? With one of these in hand, I'll be\nmuch better backup for you.
MID_LGV_0XXX_LG00_002_m11_005: <DLG>Gave Hong Hua the Salamander+3.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m03_001: A small mechanical object is buried in the sand.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m03_002: It seems to be a handheld tool of some kind. Looks\nlike it still works.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m04_001: It's an incredibly huge artificial structure. The shell\nhas been thoroughly destroyed, like a cracked egg.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m04_002: Most of what's inside is half buried by massive\namounts of sand from the desert.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m05_001: It seems to be thoroughly dried meat. I can't tell\nat a glance what animal it came from.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m05_002: It may have been left behind by the people who once\nlived here.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m06_001: This looks like a residence of some kind, but it's\nbeen abandoned for quite some time.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m06_002: It's made of firmly compacted sand. The surface is\nweathered and seems on the verge of collapse.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m07_001: It's an example of the sparse vegetation you see all\nover the desert around here.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m07_002: The climate change from the underworld leaking\nthrough has weakened it considerably.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m08: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m08_001: A huge person-shaped thing seems to have been\nparalyzed here and left for the sand to claim.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m08_002: Must be something like a golem that was made by\nthe former villagers.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m09: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m09_001: An ancient-looking device has fallen over here, left\nfor the sand to claim.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m09_002: I couldn't even guess at what it was built to do.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m10: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m10_001: It's the remains of a huge creature native to the\ndesert. There are signs of it undergoing dissection.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_002_m10_002: It looks as if it's been several years since it was\nabandoned here.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m01_001: Strange to think that I'd ever escort someone like you\nhere. Fate is funny that way.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m01_002: You must have a lot of unanswered questions about\nthe place. We have time for you to look around.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m01_003: But don't forget we're eventually due to meet up with\nFortuna in Dagsion.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m02_001: Hold it. Something's up ahead.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m02_002: Ugh... I can't believe the risen dead have found\ntheir way even here.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m02_003: The passage is too narrow to avoid them, so we'll\nhave to clear them out. Get ready for a fight.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m03_001: I think that's the last of them. We're lucky they didn't\nput up too much of a fight.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m03_002: We broke through them this time, but we should try\nto avoid unnecessary battles wherever possible.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m03_003: It's time we were on our way to Dagsion. The first\nstep is finding the exit to this cave.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m04_001: Our path is blocked, but I think we can break these\nobstacles by attacking them.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_DN00_001_m04_002: Even if they weren't in the way, sometimes you'll\nfind useful things inside. Something to keep in mind.
MID_LGV_0XXX_DN00_001_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_DN00_001_m05_001: This looks like a safe spot for a rest. If you're feeling\ntired, let's lie low here.
MID_LGV_0XXX_DN00_001_m05_002: I expect you don't have any provisions on hand,\nbut I brought some you can share.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_GM00_02_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_GM00_02_m02_001: Rare to see travelers on the road these days.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_GM00_02_m02_002: I don't know where you're headed, but there's no\ndirection you can go to escape those monsters.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_GM00_02_m02_003: You're going to Dagsion?! But it's crawling with risen\ndead! No living being should go anywhere near it.
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_GM00_02_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_GM00_02_m03_001: I can't believe you've survived this long only to go\nand throw your life away like that...
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_GM00_02_m03_002: Wait... That stark-white attire... Could you be the\nHerald of the Pale Raven?!
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_001_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_0XXX_c02_LG00_001_m01_001: Once we're past that gate we'll be in Dagsion.\nTime to find out what's waiting for us inside.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning0_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning0_m01_001: The battle against the demon god Balor's armies will\nbegin once we pass that door.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning0_m01_002: I hope your will is strong, your mind is sharp, and\nyour allies are prepared. Else we'll surely lose.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning0_m01_003: If your courage hasn't failed you, then I'll open the\ndoor for us to proceed.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning1_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning1_m01_001: My word! You've put in an impressive amount of\nwork to recruit all of the Flame Lords.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning1_m01_002: Well done! Now we have nothing to fear. Go and\nbring light to the world!
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning2_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning2_m01_001: Each Flame Lord I selected is a peerless talent—\nthe equal of a thousand warriors.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning2_m01_002: This many should be sufficient to oppose Balor.\nBut 'tis still wise to proceed with caution.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning3_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning3_m01_001: Hrm... You didn't shirk in your duty to intervene\nwhere 'twas called for.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning3_m01_002: But I still find our current forces wanting. You may\nwish to guide more warriors here before we begin.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning3_m01_003: <ICA>"Very well. I'll head back."
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning3_m01_004: <ICB>"No. We go forward."
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning3_m01_005: <ACA>The obelisks are still there for you. Unravel the\nthreads of causality and guide them to this future.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning3_m01_006: <ACB>Ah... I see you're anxious to ease the suffering of\nthose who still live.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning3_m01_007: <ACB>Very well, then. I'll not bar your way. Go forth,\nPromised One!
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_001: Wait! You have not guided a single Flame Lord to\nthis land!
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_002: To proceed without them is to choose death. For your\nown good, I beg you to reconsider.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_003: <ICA>"Very well. I'll head back."
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_004: <ICB>"No. We go forward."
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m03_001: Wait! You have not guided a single Flame Lord to\nthis land!
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m03_002: To proceed without them is to choose death. For your\nown good, I beg you to reconsider.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m03_003: What of the Flame Lords whose lives you have\ntouched, but not yet brought to this point?
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m03_004: I understand your impatience, but can you not wait\nuntil you've assembled a proper force?
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m03_005: <ICA>"Very well. I'll head back."
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m03_006: <ICB>"No. We go forward."
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m04: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_005: The obelisks are still there for you. Unravel the\nthreads of causality and guide them to this future.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_006: Is anything I've said penetrating that skull? Or are\nyou ignoring me deliberately?
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_007: Your death is certain with such paltry forces at your\nside! Please reconsider. I can't afford to lose you.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_008: <ICA>"Very well. I'll head back."
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_009: <ICB>"No. We go forward."
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m05: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_010: The obelisks are still there for you. Unravel the\nthreads of causality and guide them to this future.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m06: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m06_001: If you understand, then touch the Strife Obelisk\nand bring the Flame Lords to this place.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m07: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_011: Are you stupid? Suicidally arrogant? Or is there a\nmotive behind this that eludes me?
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Fot_Warning4_m01_012: Ye gods...fine. Do as you wish! I'll be with you to\nthe very end.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_CausationMarged_Improve_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_CausationMarged_Improve_m01_001: Causality under your guidance is much more\nfavorable. Take what you've built onward to victory!
MID_LGV_LG00_099_CausationMarged_Keep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_CausationMarged_Keep_m01_001: Now the new causality has mixed with the old.\nLead your brave warriors into the final showdown.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1Clear_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1Clear_m01_001: What was that?! Is there a new obelisk?
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1Clear_m01_007: Is that a new obelisk?
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1Clear_m01_002: Yes. 'Tis a touchstone leading to a pivotal point\nin time...the Strife Obelisk.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1Clear_m01_003: You've now intervened in causality for one warrior.\nMasterfully done, I must say.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1Clear_m01_004: But there's one final push we must make before they\ncan join us here.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1Clear_m01_005: Touch that obelisk and discover the path leading\nthem to our present day.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1Clear_m01_006: It is the final link in the chain of causality that shall\nlead your Flame Lord here!
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1NoClear_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1NoClear_m01_001: Ah, you've returned. How does it feel to have\nbrushed with causality so?
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1NoClear_m01_002: This Obelisk Chamber is a place suffused with the\npower of the Goddess of Fate—mine, in other words.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1NoClear_m01_003: There are other ways to tinker with causality here.\nTouch a few things and see for yourself.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1NoClear_m01_004: For instance, if you touch the same obelisk again,\nyou can watch causality play out once more.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1NoClear_m01_005: Or touch a new one to see how cause and effect\nintertwine in another's life.
MID_LGV_LG00_099_Part1NoClear_m01_006: The means are mine, but the method is yours.\nUse them as you see fit.